 test tests/DcaShop.IntegrationTests --logger trx 2>&1 | grep -E \"Passed!|Failed!\" ; dotnet test tests/DcaShop.ArchitectureTests 2>&1 | grep -E \"Passed!|Failed!\" ; dotnet test tests/DcaShop.E2eTests --logger trx 2>&1 | grep -E \"Passed!|Failed!\"","timeout":600000}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_014cTZpgYnQvTJCa48CJe3pY","tool_input":{"command":"for p in UnitTests IntegrationTests ArchitectureTests E2eTests; do echo \"== $p\"; dotnet test tests/DcaShop.$p --logger trx 2>&1 | tail -4; done","timeout":600000}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":18,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I finished the tidy stage for `pay-through-the-provider` and wrote the result to `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/tidy.md`. It changes one thing and no behaviour.\n\n**The one change:** in `src/DcaShop.Checkout/Infrastructure/CheckoutContextRegistration.cs`, the inline code that adds a trailing slash to the provider's address is now a small private method, `WithTrailingSlash(Uri)`. The comment explaining why the slash is needed moved onto that method. No other files and no tests were touched.\n\n**Left alone and noted in the file:**\n- Both the use case and the REST adapter log an unavailable payment. The build notes say this is on purpose; whether one log line would do is a question for the judge.\n- The use case checks the payment outcome twice. A switch would be shorter, but it would have to repeat a guard for an authorized payment that comes back without a reference.\n- The REST adapter answers a cancellation with `Refused`, when \"not supported\" is what it means. That's a question about the port's contract, not a tidy-up.\n\n**Checks, all run after the change:**\n- Build: no errors.\n- Tests: unit 178 passed (4 skipped), integration 65 passed (1 skipped), architecture 129 passed, E2E 38 passed (1 skipped). Nothing failed.\n- Formatter: clean.\n\nI ran no other stage.","ttft_ms":3238,"type":"result","duration_ms":191050,"uuid":"5e155821-2563-45e9-a044-3d7151caa257","ttft_stream_ms":2298,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":2298,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
